cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use XPP Lab in your work, please cite it as below, and cite
  XPPAUT itself, whose methods it runs (the reference below).
type: software
title: XPP Lab
abstract: >-
  XPPAUT 8.0's simulation and AUTO bifurcation engine, with the same
  numbers as XPPAUT, as a desktop app for Windows, macOS and Linux and as a
  Python package.
authors:
  - given-names: César Eduardo
    family-names: Perdomo Díaz
version: 0.1.1
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/CesarPerdomoDiaz/xpplab"
url: "https://cesarperdomodiaz.github.io/xpplab/"
keywords:
  - XPPAUT
  - AUTO
  - bifurcation analysis
  - dynamical systems
  - ordinary differential equations
  - computational neuroscience
references:
  - type: book
    title: >-
      Simulating, Analyzing, and Animating Dynamical Systems: A Guide to
      XPPAUT for Researchers and Students
    authors:
      - given-names: Bard
        family-names: Ermentrout
    publisher:
      name: SIAM
    year: 2002
